{"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"kind":"attribute","text":"@discardableResult"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"authenticateDevice","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"() ","kind":"text"},{"text":"async","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"throws","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" -> ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:8AxiamSDK0A6ClientC","identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/AxiamClient","text":"AxiamClient","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:8AxiamSDK0A6ClientC17DeviceLoginResultV","identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/AxiamClient\/DeviceLoginResult","text":"DeviceLoginResult","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"platforms":["Linux"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"text":"Discussion","type":"heading","anchor":"discussion","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Issues ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"POST \/api\/v1\/auth\/device"},{"text":" with no request body.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Reachable only on a client configured with a client certificate","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" (rule 7,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/AxiamConfig\/clientCertificate","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"). On any other client this refuses"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"CLIENT-SIDE with "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/AxiamError\/auth(_:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"zero wire calls"}]},{"type":"text","text":": without a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"certificate the server would answer "},{"code":"401","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" regardless, so going to the wire would"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"only turn a configuration mistake into an authentication failure."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"On success the returned token is ","type":"text"},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"adopted as this client’s credential"}]},{"text":", exactly","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"as a ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"login()"},{"text":" result is (rule 6): every subsequent REST call this client sends —","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"including every ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"management()"},{"text":" operation — carries it as ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Authorization: Bearer <token>"},{"text":" and withholds this client’s own cookie jar, so a session cookie from an","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"earlier ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"login()"},{"text":" can never ride alongside it. The server reads the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"axiam_access"},{"text":" cookie before ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Authorization"},{"text":", so keeping a stale one would","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"silently run every later request as the ","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"previous","type":"text"}]},{"text":" session’s principal, defeating","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the point of authenticating fresh.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"There is no refresh token"}]},{"text":" for this credential (rule 6, D-6 of the dogfooding","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"plan): the §9 single-flight guard has nothing to spend on it, so a later ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"401"},{"text":" —","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"on this call, or on any request this client sends afterward — is surfaced as","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/AuthError"},{"text":" with ","type":"text"},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"no refresh attempt"}]},{"text":". The caller recovers by calling","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"authenticateDevice()"},{"text":" again, which costs one TLS handshake.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Every refusal is a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"401"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" (rule 8, server T22.4): an unknown, untrusted,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"expired, revoked or unbound certificate, and a ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Server"},{"text":"-type certificate, all map","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"to ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/AuthError","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":". A ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"429"},{"text":" from the route’s per-IP rate limiter maps to","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/NetworkError","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" (§2), never ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/AuthError","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" — ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"mapError"},{"text":" already keeps the two","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"apart, so this method adds no special-casing for it, and it is never retried","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"here.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The token is "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"certificate-bound"}]},{"type":"text","text":" ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"cnf.x5t#S256"},{"type":"text","text":") when AXIAM itself terminated"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the TLS handshake (rule 9); "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DeviceLoginResult.tokenType"},{"type":"text","text":" stays "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"\"Bearer\""},{"type":"text","text":" either"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"way. A resource server verifying it locally MUST use"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AxiamRequestAuthenticator.authenticateSenderConstrained(_:presentedThumbprint:)"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"(or thread "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PresentedProofs"},{"type":"text","text":" through "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"authenticate(_:presentedProofs:)"},{"type":"text","text":") rather"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"than the plain "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"authenticate(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":", which — after this SDK’s own §10.1 rule 9 fix"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"— refuses a bound token with no evidence."}]},{"name":"Throws","type":"aside","style":"note","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":""},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/AxiamError\/auth(_:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" client-side (no certificate configured, zero"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"wire calls) or from the server’s "},{"code":"401","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"; "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/AxiamError\/network(_:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" for a "},{"code":"429","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"or any other non-"},{"code":"200","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}]}],"kind":"content"}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/